Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: use the GMU recovery shutdown path after a GPU hang

The GPU recovery worker marks the GPU hung before invoking runtime
suspend. Use the existing forced GMU shutdown while that flag is set,
so a stuck GPU does not have to finish the graceful slumber request.
Preserve the bus vote, GX, clock and runtime PM release order.

Link: https://github.com/wkai343/liuqin-linux-kit/blob/9b8e38fd75008f5d4bec912acb1a0331aa112047/build/kernel/patches/linux-7.3/0081-drm-msm-bound-fault-dump-waits.patch
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1510,7 +1510,7 @@ int a6xx_gmu_stop(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	 * Force the GMU off if we detected a hang, otherwise try to shut it
 	 * down gracefully
 	 */
-	if (gmu->hung)
+	if (gmu->hung || a6xx_gpu->hung)
 		a6xx_gmu_force_off(gmu);
 	else
 		a6xx_gmu_shutdown(gmu);
